## Ascribe documentation

The Markdown pages under `docs/` are Ascribe documentation: pages with YAML frontmatter, `@` directives, and `{key}` phrases, checked against the content model in `ascribe.toml`.

Programmatic check: after editing a page, run `ascribe check <file> --format concise` and fix every error. Before you finish, run `ascribe check`. `ascribe explain <code>` says what a problem means and how to fix it.

Before writing a page about a subject, run `ascribe search "<words>"` to find where the pages already say it, as readers read them, and link to what's there or extend it instead of saying it again.

Read a block's `@memo` before changing the block, and keep the two together: a memo says why the page is written the way it is, and is never published.

`ascribe outline <page>` lists the memo files about a page and each of its headings: read a memo before changing the block it's about, and keep it.

### Page types

A page says what type it is with `type:` in its frontmatter, first, and its other fields are its type's. A file or folder whose name starts with `_` is a fragment, which pages `@include`, not a page, and names no type.

- `page`: frontmatter `title` (string, required), `description` (string)

### Phrases

Write the phrase (`{product}`), not the text it stands for.

- `{product}`: Quill
- `{cloud}`: Quill Cloud
- `{version}`: 3.4.1
- `{api}`: https://api.quill.dev/v3/

### Directives this project uses

- `@id: <id>` on the line under a heading: an id for links to it that doesn't change with its text
- `@include: <file>.md`, or `@include: <file>.md#<id>` for one section: another file's content, in place
- `@variant {<dimension>=<value>}:` before each arm, and one `@end` after the last: content that differs by a dimension. Here: dimensions `pm`, `deployment`
- `@available: <spec>` under a heading or above a block: where it applies, as targets with an optional state and version (`cloud, self-managed preview 3.4`), or a feature's key
- `@note {type=<type>}: <text>`, or `@note:` … `@end` around several blocks: a callout. Here: types `note`, `tip`, `important`, `warning`, `caution`
- `@steps` on the line above an ordered list: the list is a procedure
- `@memo: <text>` under a heading or above a block, or `@memo:` … `@end` around several lines: a note for whoever maintains the page, never published

### Links

Link to the source file, with a relative path such as `../guides/install.md#configure`, not to the site's address. `ascribe outline <page>` lists a page's headings with their ids, and `ascribe link <target> --from <page>` says whether a link works and what to write. A product's message that links to these docs by a permalink can read what the docs will show for it first: `ascribe resolve go:<name>` prints the help a product shows, from the build's `help.json`. Give a heading with a permalink a summary, a sentence or two a product shows with its help: `@summary` on the line above a paragraph of the section that reads well alone, or `@summary: <text>` under the heading and its `@id` when none does, as for a lead-in to a list. Keep it under 300 characters.

### More

`ascribe model` shows everything the content model allows. Every directive: https://ascribed-dev.com/go/directives/
